@hl:    mov16 qx, px
        mov16 qy, py
        add16i qy, 16

argument:
@stepn is the 'q1 is negative, step up a slope' arm of the per-pixel horizontal move loop, reached from `lda q1 / bmi @stepn`; it runs once per horizontal pixel of movement while climbing. `lda py+1 / adc #$FF / sta py+1` is the usual conditional-decrement idiom: with C set it rewrites py+1 unchanged, with C clear it decrements. Since the preceding `adc py` only clears C when the low byte of py is 0, C is set 255 times out of 256, and in that overwhelmingly common case the three instructions are pure cost.

Replacing them with `bcs` to the existing shared tail costs: original after `sta py` = lda py+1 (3) + adc #$FF (2) + sta py+1 (3) + stz alt (3) + bra @hnext (3) = 14; proposal, C set = bcs taken (3) + stz alt (3) + bra @hnext (3) = 9, saving 5. C clear = 2 + dec py+1 (5) + bra taken (3) + 3 + 3 = 16, losing 2 on 1 execution in 256. Net +5 per @stepn.

Anonymous labels: this adds two references to the existing ':' on the `stza alt` line but adds and removes no ':' line, so the label count through player_update is unchanged - `:-` binds to the nearest preceding anonymous label, which is that one (nothing between it and the branches defines another). Flags/registers: `dec py+1` sets N,Z from the result instead of the old `sta`'s no-op, but the tail is `stz alt / bra @hnext / lda dpx+1`, none of which reads them; C is likewise dead. A now still holds q1 rather than py+1 at the tail, and A is reloaded at @hnext. Bytes: 10 -> 6.

